# File & Folder Organization

## Top-level source layout (`src/`)

```zsh
src/
├── app/        ← Next.js routes only — thin files (import + re-export, no logic)
├── features/   ← All business-logic components; imported via '@/features' barrel
├── ui/         ← UI primitives and design system; imported via '@/ui' barrel
├── ui-theme/   ← MUI theme (TEMPORARY — will be deleted in Phase 4 migration)
├── alerts/     ← Effector-based alert system
├── config/     ← Metadata, mocks, constants
├── lib/        ← auth, db, email, swagger, validations, utils
├── stores/     ← Effector stores
├── utils/      ← Pure utility functions
└── types/      ← Shared TypeScript types
```

## `app/` — Thin routes

Every `page.tsx` must be a thin file: **import + re-export only**.

```tsx
// ✅ correct
import { SomePage } from '@/features'
export { someMetadata as metadata } from '@/config'
export default SomePage

// ❌ wrong — no JSX, no logic, no data fetching in page.tsx
```

- `layout.tsx` and `route.ts` (API routes) may contain setup code
- Co-location of route-specific modules in the route folder is allowed only for API routes

## `features/` — Business logic components

All components with site-specific logic (auth state, DB calls, domain behavior):

```zsh
features/
├── home/            home sections + HomePage
├── dashboard/       DashboardPage (async Server Component)
├── auth/            LoginForm, LoginPage
├── onboarding/      OnboardingWizard, SignupPage
├── portfolio/       Portfolio, PortfolioEditor, portfolio-item, portfolio-viewer
├── freelancer-profile/  editor, public view, FreelancerProfilePage
├── playground/      PlaygroundPage + all demo components
├── header.tsx
├── footer.tsx
├── db-health-alert.tsx
└── index.ts         ← barrel — always import from '@/features'
```

Always import via barrel: `import { X } from '@/features'`

## `ui/` — Primitives & design system

All reusable UI components with no business logic:

```zsh
ui/
├── shadcn/          ← raw Radix/shadcn components (INTERNAL — never import directly)
├── providers/       ← ThemeRegistry, FontProvider
├── icons/           ← custom SVG icons
├── button.tsx
├── icon.tsx
├── icon-button.tsx
├── link.tsx
├── stack.tsx
├── text-styled.tsx
├── file-uploader.tsx
├── assets.tsx
└── index.ts         ← barrel — always import from '@/ui'
```

### Import rules

```tsx
// ✅ Always use the barrel
import { Button, Icon, TS, Label, Separator } from '@/ui'

// ❌ Never import from shadcn directly
import { Button } from '@/ui/shadcn/button'   // FORBIDDEN

// ❌ Never import from ui sub-paths for items in the barrel
import { Button } from '@/ui/button'           // prefer barrel unless justified
```

All shadcn components that don't have a custom wrapper are re-exported from `ui/index.ts`.
New shadcn installs: add the component to `ui/shadcn/`, then re-export it from `ui/index.ts`.

## Flat structure preference

- Prefer flat folders over deep nesting
- Use prefix-based grouping for related files: `demo.tsx`, `demo-buttons.tsx`, `demo-icons.tsx`
- Create subfolders only when there are 5+ related files forming a distinct domain

## Barrel hygiene

Barrel files (`index.ts`) export only the public API of a module:

- Self-contained page/section components
- Pure UI primitives
- Types and constants

Internal sub-components (those receiving callback props from a parent, or only meaningful as children of a specific component) stay as relative imports and are NOT exported from the barrel.

See `.cursor/rules/use-client.mdc` for how barrel exports interact with `'use client'` directives.

## When to add a subfolder

Only when all of these are true:
1. More than 5 files in the group
2. The group has a distinct domain (e.g. `freelancer-profile`, `onboarding`)
3. The group has its own `index.ts` barrel
